      "content": "that most of those \"benefits\" sound like they're just excuses for why the majority of voters don't actually matter in the end. if a system makes it so a candidate can win even when most people voted against them, isn't that fundamentally broken? like, how can anyone say that's actually \"good for democracy\" when it literally contradicts the core idea of one person one vote?",
